Third-party data and software
-----------------------------
The full register of every dataset, model, tool, voice, font, music track and image, with its
licence, commercial-use status and attribution, is docs/licences.md (machine-readable copy:
docs/licences.csv). This file mirrors the attributions that must travel with the code; the
full generated credits are docs/credits.md, and the generated block at the end of this file lists
every register item whose row names an attribution (`make credits` rebuilds both).

OpenStreetMap
  Rail, road and place data are derived from OpenStreetMap data, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
  available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Extracts are obtained from Geofabrik GmbH (https://download.geofabrik.de/). Derived databases
  remain subject to the ODbL (share-alike); every map credits "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors".
  No OSM extract is committed to this repository (data/ is gitignored).

GASTAT open data
  Population, census and transport statistics come from the General Authority for Statistics of
  the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (GASTAT), https://www.stats.gov.sa/ , used under its open-data terms
  of use, with attribution to GASTAT. Tables derived or modified here are marked as derived and
  are not official GASTAT statistics.

TrafficTwin Jeddah
  Conventions, orchestration scripts, agents, skills and the Jeddah coupling are adapted from
  TrafficTwin Jeddah, (c) 2026 The TrafficTwin Jeddah contributors, Apache License 2.0 (the
  author's optional private companion project: not public, and not required to run, test or
  reproduce this repository). Its derived Jeddah network
  (data/jeddah/jeddah.v2.net.xml, used through a local symlink and not redistributed) is a
  derived database of OpenStreetMap under the ODbL.

Population grids, buildings and imagery (R1a, GEO_VERIFY)
