Eclipse SUMO and OSRM (R4)
  The Jeddah decongestion coupling runs Eclipse SUMO 1.28.0, (c) German Aerospace Center (DLR) and
  others, Eclipse Public License 2.0 (https://eclipse.dev/sumo/), from the read-only TrafficTwin
  environment, as a dependency, not vendored. Road skims use OSRM (osrm-backend, BSD-2-Clause).

Network, pilgrims and alignments (R4)
  Pilgrim tables: Source: General Authority for Statistics (GASTAT), Umrah Statistics and Hajj
  Statistics (with MoHU, MoI and Jeddah Islamic Port as data owners); General Authority of Civil
  Aviation (GACA) press release; Saudi Press Agency (SPA), relaying SAR. Derived tables are marked
  as derived. Domestic air routes: Wikipedia contributors, CC BY-SA 4.0 (airport pages, read
  1 Nov 2026). Alignment cost surface: ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus
  Sentinel data (2021) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium (CC BY 4.0); OpenStreetMap layers
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0; geology from Pollastro, R.M., 1998, USGS (public
  domain); terrain produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 (see the R3 block). WDPA is not used
  (non-commercial terms). The committed alignment sidecars (cities/ksa/alignments/) are treated as
  ODbL share-alike until their release status is decided.

Appraisal parameters (R5)
  Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0 (Department
  for Transport, TAG Data Book v2.03 and TAG units A1.1, A1.3, A2.1, A2.4; HM Treasury, The Green
  Book; Department for Energy Security and Net Zero, greenhouse gas conversion factors and carbon
  values). (c) European Union; source: European Commission, Handbook on the external costs of
  transport (CE Delft, 2019). Our World in Data, based on Ember and Energy Institute (CC BY 4.0).
  International Monetary Fund, World Economic Outlook Database, October 2026 (IMF terms; reuse
  terms to check before release). Saudi Global Ports, intermodal dry-port tariff announcement
  (terms not stated; cited only, enters no result). Values are transcribed with citations; no
  table is redistributed.

Third-party software (dependencies, not vendored)
  Python (installed by uv from uv.lock): pyyaml, pydantic, numpy, pandas, pyarrow, duckdb,
  shapely, pyproj, geopandas, pyogrio, networkx, typer, rich, scipy, matplotlib, httpx, rasterio (its wheel
  bundles GDAL) and their dependencies, under permissive licences (MIT, BSD-2/3-Clause, Apache-2.0, ISC, PSF-2.0,
  MIT-CMU, the matplotlib licence) except certifi (MPL-2.0, unmodified). Dev only: ruff (MIT),
  pytest (MIT). Per-package versions and licences are in docs/licences.md.

Synthetic demand
  All modelled results are labelled "synthetic demand, uncalibrated: scenario comparison, not a
  forecast" until calibration says otherwise. Cost and benefit figures are P10/P50/P90 ranges.

Decision dashboard (R8: api/, web/)
  The dashboard reuses the Vite + React + deck.gl + MapLibre viewer and FastAPI patterns of
  TrafficTwin Jeddah, (c) 2026 The TrafficTwin Jeddah contributors, Apache License 2.0
  (optional private companion project, not public): web/tsconfig.json is copied; web/vite.config.ts,
  web/scripts/screenshot.mjs (from scripts/lib.mjs), web/src/components/MapView.tsx (from
  src/engine.ts), api/settings.py and api/main.py are adapted. Python: FastAPI (MIT), Starlette
  (BSD-3-Clause), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), opentelemetry-api (Apache-2.0). JavaScript, bundled in
  web/dist (not committed): React and react-dom (MIT), deck.gl (MIT, (c) vis.gl contributors),
  MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause, (c) MapLibre contributors), Noto Sans and Noto Naskh Arabic via
  Fontsource (SIL Open Font License 1.1); build and dev tools Vite (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0),
  puppeteer-core (Apache-2.0). Basemap: OpenFreeMap (https://openfreemap.org, MIT), (c)
  OpenMapTiles (code BSD-3-Clause, design CC BY 4.0), Positron style (code BSD-3-Clause, design
  CC BY 4.0, derived from CARTO basemaps, CC BY 3.0), data from OpenStreetMap, (c) OpenStreetMap
  contributors, ODbL 1.0; the OSM credit is always visible on the map and in every screenshot.
  Per-package versions and licences: docs/licences.md (R8 rows; the track fragment was folded
  in at INTEGRATE_R8).

